+# Migrating from v1.2 to v1.3
+
+v1.3 is additive within the stable version-one contract. `API_LEVEL` remains
+`1`, `NUMERICAL_CONTRACT` remains `validated-v1`, and the curated `prelude` is
+unchanged. Existing v1.2 imports require no source changes.
+
+## New specialized modules
+
+- `discriminant`: empirical-prior LDA and QDA with explicit covariance ridge.
+- `canonical_correlation`: covariance-whitened canonical variates.
+- `manova`: one-factor Wilks/Pillai summaries and seeded permutation inference.
+- `partial_correlation`: precision matrices and all-other-variable partial correlations.
+- `copula`: Gaussian copulas fitted from empirical marginal ranks.
+- `censored_regression`: shared-boundary Gaussian left/right Tobit regression.
+- `mediation`: linear path decomposition with Sobel and percentile-bootstrap evidence.
+- `clustering`: seeded k-means++ and bounded pairwise silhouette scoring.
+- `forecast_evaluation`: MASE/RMSSE/sMAPE and Diebold-Mariano tests.
+- `survival_scoring`: Harrell concordance and IPCW Brier scoring.
+
+Import these from the crate root or their modules. They are deliberately not
+added to the conservative v1 `prelude`.
+
+## Assumption changes to make explicit
+
+No existing defaults changed. New callers should declare:
+
+- covariance regularization for discriminant, CCA, MANOVA, partial-correlation,
+  and copula models;
+- exchangeability for MANOVA permutations and mediation bootstrap rows;
+- one shared censoring boundary and Gaussian latent errors for Tobit models;
+- linear no-unmeasured-confounding interpretation before calling mediation
+  effects causal;
+- cluster count, seed, and Euclidean geometry for k-means;
+- seasonal-naive scale and HAC bandwidth for forecast comparison;
+- independent censoring and calibrated survival probabilities for IPCW scores.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run `scripts/verify.sh` under Rust 1.85+ and separately run
+`scripts/verify_v1_3_references.sh` in an environment with NumPy, SciPy,
+scikit-learn, and statsmodels.
