 - Pinball, expectile, interval, and CRPS values are comparative proper or
   task-specific scores. Their magnitude depends on the outcome scale and should
   be reported against meaningful baselines on held-out observations.
+
+## v1.3 multivariate, censored, and predictive scope
+
+- LDA uses an unbiased pooled within-class covariance and empirical priors. QDA
+  uses one unbiased covariance per class. Ridge terms are explicit modeling
+  regularizers; posterior probabilities inherit Gaussian class assumptions.
+- Canonical correlation whitens sample covariance blocks through symmetric
+  eigendecomposition. Near-singular blocks require an explicit ridge, and
+  canonical directions are descriptive rather than causal.
+- MANOVA reports Wilks' lambda and Pillai's trace from one-factor SSCP matrices.
+  Seeded permutation p-values require exchangeable group labels. Ridge changes
+  the tested geometry and must be reported.
+- Partial correlations are derived from a regularized Gaussian precision
+  matrix. Zero partial correlation implies conditional independence only under
+  suitable joint-distribution assumptions.
+- Gaussian copulas use empirical average ranks divided by `n+1` and shrink
+  off-diagonal latent correlations toward independence. Marginal distributions
+  are not estimated or transformed back by this module.
+- Tobit regression assumes one common left or right censoring boundary,
+  Gaussian homoskedastic latent errors, and correct linear specification. The
+  deterministic gradient optimizer fails closed on non-convergence.
+- Linear mediation estimates ordinary least-squares path products. Sobel
+  inference is asymptotic and percentile bootstrap intervals assume row-level
+  exchangeability. Causal mediation additionally requires untestable treatment,
+  mediator, and outcome confounding assumptions.
+- K-means minimizes Euclidean within-cluster squared distance and can identify
+  local optima. The seed fixes k-means++ initialization; silhouette calculation
+  is quadratic and explicitly bounded.
+- MASE and RMSSE scale against a caller-declared seasonal-naive training
+  baseline. Diebold-Mariano inference uses a Bartlett HAC estimate and its
+  asymptotic normal approximation.
+- Harrell concordance ignores pairs that are not comparable under right
+  censoring. Brier scores use Kaplan-Meier inverse censoring weights and require
+  independent censoring plus non-increasing survival predictions.
